tly, and do not create your own subclasses of this class. The shape","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"classes correspond to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Geometry","type":"text"},{"text":" object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types in the GeoJSON standard, but some have nonstandard names for backwards","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compatibility.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Although you do not create instances of this class directly, you can use its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape\/shapeWithData:encoding:error:","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" factory method to create one of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"concrete subclasses of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" noted above from GeoJSON data. To access a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shape’s attributes, use the corresponding ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNFeature","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" class instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add shapes to the map by adding them to an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Configure the appearance of an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s or ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shapes collectively using a concrete instance of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Alternatively, you can add some kinds of shapes directly to a map view as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"annotations or overlays.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can filter the features in a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or vary their layout or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paint attributes based on the features’ geographies. Pass an "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSPredicate"},{"type":"text","text":" with the format "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SELF IN %@"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"%@ CONTAINS SELF"},{"type":"text","text":" and set the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer\/predicate","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property to that predicate, or set a layout or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"paint attribute to a similarly formatted "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSExpression"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolygon":{"title":"MLNPolygon","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolygon","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" object represents a closed shape consisting of four or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, specified as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D"},{"type":"text","text":" instances, and the edges that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connect them. For example, you could use a polygon shape to represent a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"building, a lake, or an area you want to highlight."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNVectorStyleLayer":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MLNVectorStyleLayer","abstract":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer"},{"text":" is an abstract superclass for style layers whose content","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is defined by an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer","fragments":[{"text":"MLNVectorStyleLayer","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnvectorstylelayer","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/objc(pl)NSSecureCoding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/objc(pl)NSSecureCoding","title":"NSSecureCoding","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNShapeCollectionFeature":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollectionFeature"},{"text":" object associates a shape collection with an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"optional identifier and attributes.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeCollectionFeature","fragments":[{"text":"MLNShapeCollectionFeature","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnshapecollectionfeature","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolyline":{"title":"MLNPolyline","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPolyline","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolyline","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of two or more vertices,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified as ","type":"text"},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances, and the line segments that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connect them. For example, you could use an polyline to represent a road or the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"path along which something moves."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNVectorStyleLayer/predicate":{"kind":"symbol","title":"predicate","abstract":[{"text":"The style layer’s predicate.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer\/predicate","fragments":[{"text":"predicate","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnvectorstylelayer\/predicate","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPolylineFeature":{"title":"MLNPolylineFeature","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNPolylineFeature"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolylinefeature","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolylineFeature"},{"text":" object associates a polyline shape with an optional","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifier and attributes.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolylineFeature","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS/GeoJSON":{"kind":"article","title":"Working with GeoJSON Data","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GeoJSON","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre-native-for-ios\/geojson","type":"topic","role":"article"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNAnnotation":{"title":"MLNAnnotation","fragments":[{"text":"MLNAnnotation","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnannotation","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol is used to provide annotation-related information"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a map view. To use this protocol, you adopt it in any custom objects that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"store or represent annotation data. Each object then serves as the source of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"information about a single map annotation and provides critical information,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"such as the annotation’s location on the map. Annotation objects do not provide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the visual representation of the annotation but typically coordinate (in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"conjunction with the map view’s delegate) the creation of an appropriate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"objects to handle the display."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNAnnotation","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNVectorTileSource":{"title":"MLNVectorTileSource","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNVectorTileSource"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnvectortilesource","type":"topic","abstract":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" is a map content source that supplies tiled vector data"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"text","text":"Mapbox Vector Tile"},{"type":"text","text":" format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"to be shown on the map. The location of and metadata about the tiles are","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defined either by an option dictionary or by an external file that conforms to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TileJSON specification"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A vector tile source is added to an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyle"},{"type":"text","text":" object along with one or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorStyleLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" objects. A vector style layer defines the appearance of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any content supplied by the vector tile source."}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/objc(cs)NSObject":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/objc(cs)NSObject","title":"NSObject","type":"unresolvable"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNShapeSource":{"title":"MLNShapeSource","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNShapeSource"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnshapesource","abstract":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource"},{"text":" is a map content source that supplies vector shapes to be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"shown on the map. The shapes may be instances of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShape"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or they may be defined by local or external","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"GeoJSON","type":"text"},{"text":" code. A shape source is added to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyle"},{"text":" object along with an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyle"},{"text":" object. The vector style","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"layer defines the appearance of any content supplied by the shape source. You","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can update a shape source by setting its ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"shape"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"text":" property.","type":"text"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNStyle":{"title":"MLNStyle","fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNStyle"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnstyle","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The proxy object for the current map style.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNStyle","kind":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNPointCollection":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPointCollection","title":"MLNPointCollection","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"MLNPointCollection","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpointcollection","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPointCollection","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"disconnected vertices, specified as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D"},{"type":"text","text":" instances. The"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"points in the collection may be related but are not connected spatially. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, you could use a point collection to represent all the trees in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"orchard.","type":"text"}]},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNMultiPolyline":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MLNMultiPolyline","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polylines. For example, you could use a multipolyline shape to represent both","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sides of a divided highway (dual carriageway), excluding the median (central","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reservation): each carriageway would be a distinct ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline"},{"text":" object.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolyline","fragments":[{"text":"MLNMultiPolyline","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnmultipolyline","type":"topic","role":"symbol"},"doc://org.swift.MyProject/documentation/MapLibre/MLNMultiPolygon":{"kind":"symbol","title":"MLNMultiPolygon","abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon"},{"text":" object represents a shape consisting of one or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polygons that do not overlap. For example, you could use a multipolygon shape","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to represent the body of land that consists of an island surrounded by an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"atoll: the inner island would be one ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"text":" object, while the surrounding","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"atoll would be another. You could also use a multipolygon shape to represent a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group of disconnected but related buildings.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon","fragments":[{"text":"MLNMultiPolygon","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnmultipolygon